Packaging notes for code-on-incus
=================================

Go 1.25 toolchain
-----------------
go.mod requires Go 1.25. Availability of `golang-1.25-go` differs per series:

  * resolute (26.04)  - in the archive (universe). No PPA needed.
  * noble   (24.04)   - NOT in the archive; needs the backports PPA.
  * jammy   (22.04)   - NOT in the archive; needs the backports PPA.

For the two LTS series that lack it, the toolchain comes from:

    ppa:longsleep/golang-backports   (package: golang-1.25-go)

Launchpad's builders have no internet access, so the toolchain cannot be
downloaded at build time. Instead, this PPA must declare the backports PPA as
an *archive dependency* so the builders can resolve `golang-1.25-go`:

  1. Open your PPA on Launchpad -> "View package details" -> "Edit dependencies".
  2. Add "PPA for Simon Eisenmann - Golang Backports"
     (ppa:longsleep/golang-backports).
  3. Save. Re-trigger any failed builds.

Vendored modules
----------------
The builders also cannot fetch Go modules, so they are vendored. Regenerate
before building a source package:

    go mod vendor

vendor/ is intentionally NOT committed to git (see .gitignore); it is produced
as a build prerequisite locally and in CI, and dpkg-source includes it in the
(native-format) source tarball that is uploaded.

Source format
-------------
This uses "3.0 (native)" for simplicity on a personal PPA: one tarball, no
orig/patch split. If this is ever submitted to the Debian archive, switch to
"3.0 (quilt)" with a separate upstream orig tarball.
